<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 25 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 25 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 25 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    400 MLN    400 MLN    400 MLN    400 MLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    150 MLN*   340 MLN*   365 MLN</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  T-BILLS	=	    120 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	     30 MLN*   =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS				 190 MLN*</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  25 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
